{"availability":"available","full":"Debapriya-source/nyaya-gpt","name":"nyaya-gpt","description":"AI agent with RAG+ReAct  on Indian Constitution & BNS","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":83,"forks":18,"created":"2024-09-10T22:20:25Z","updated":"2026-03-25T19:25:47Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://nyaya-gpt.streamlit.app/","topics":["artificial-intelligence","groq","llama3-1","llm","rag","streamlit"],"demo":"https://nyaya-gpt.streamlit.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T05:50:07.677Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T05:50:07.677Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T05:50:07.677Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T13:35:25.817Z","stars":83,"forks":18},{"at":"2026-10-09T05:50:07.677Z","stars":83,"forks":18}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Let’s dive into some advanced AI concepts with a real-world problem like building a smart legal assistant, Nyaya-GPT. This project helps users to query legal documents like the Indian Constitution and Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS) with precision. We'll explore concepts like ReAct, RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) and Vector Databases and how they work together to push the boundaries of simple fact retrieval.","Now, this is where ReAct (Reason + Act) steps in to supercharge our naive RAG. Instead of just pulling up facts, ReAct allows the model to reason through a query and then act to retrieve relevant info in multiple steps. It uses a \"think before you act\" kind of approach, where the agent breaks down the query, performs actions (like retrieving data), and refines the answer before responding."],"features":["Query Understanding: It doesn’t just do a blind search—it thinks about what you're asking. If the first attempt isn't great, it revises its actions.","Multi-step Reasoning: Rather than fetching a single fact, it performs multiple steps to ensure the answer is accurate and contextually appropriate.","Error Handling and Mem